<Base title='Privacy and your choices'><div class="container"><div class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">The publication</p><h1>Privacy and your choices</h1></div><article class="prose section"><p>This preview disables live newsletter subscriptions, analytics and advertising. The contact form may send information to Netlify when its processing is enabled; form storage and owner email notifications are separate services.</p><h2>Information on this device</h2><p>Saved campground IDs, checklist entries, cost estimates and analytics preferences can be stored in your browser. They are device-specific, do not sync to an account and can be cleared using the tools or browser settings. Shareable budget links include numeric costs only; directory filter links can contain the selected filters and search terms.</p><h2>Optional analytics</h2><p>When a production analytics integration is configured, the site uses a basic consent model: no analytics requests before acceptance. You can reject analytics or change your choice using Privacy preferences in the footer. Analytics sends allowlisted event context and canonical page paths, not email addresses, contact messages or query strings. It is not a complete visitor census.</p><h2>Newsletter and inquiries</h2><p>When enabled, newsletter email and selected interests are sent through our server-side adapter to the explicitly selected Beehiiv publication. Allowlisted campaign context, page and signup placement may accompany a new subscription. Existing subscriptions are not rewritten by repeat requests. Unsubscribe using the provider’s email links.</p><p>Contact information is intended only to answer inquiries, investigate corrections and prevent abuse. Do not submit payment information or sensitive personal records. Before production launch the owner must confirm a privacy contact, access procedures and a retention period; a proposed 90-day inquiry review policy is documented for approval and is not an automated deletion service.</p><h2>External services</h2><p>Netlify hosts the site and may process request and security logs under its own service policies. Maps load OpenStreetMap tiles only after you open the map, sharing ordinary request information with that service. External booking and rental sites have their own policies. This page must be reviewed against the final production configuration before release.</p></article></div></Base>
